            <ArticleTitle>Chronic pain related to first bite syndrome: report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>154-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjoms.2009.10.035</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>First bite syndrome is the classic symptomatology of pain in the parotid region that occurs in response to the first bite of a meal. We report two cases of this syndrome in patients after operations to the parapharyngeal space.</AbstractText>
